 "track": "D - honest statistics for the data confrontation (Fig 8)",
 "verdict": "The two-clone strip kernel does NOT reproduce control mouse-oesophagus clone-size dynamics: after an explicit measurement layer fitted on the 1-month control arm, the out-of-sample residual KS grows monotonically with age (0.057 at 3 mo, 0.171 at 6 mo, 0.276 at 12 mo; critical ~0.02) because the model coarsens as t^~0.8 while the tissue's median clone area saturates after 3 months. Every one of 24 published data-vs-kernel comparisons is formally rejected, and load never rescues the fit. The manuscript's load signal (KS 0.04-0.09) and its 600-3,200-clone power prescription are a mean-rescaling discretization artifact; 80% discrimination power is reached only at 12 months and s_d >= 5e-3 (n80 ~730-18,000/arm); elsewhere power stays below 80% up to 51,200 clones/arm (max 0.52 at s_d=1e-2/6mo, 0.23 at s_d<=2e-3/3mo, otherwise near the 0.05 size).",
